'''Robin Byron Lopez''' (born April 1, 1988) is an American former professional [[basketball]] player in the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). He was selected with the 15th pick in the [[2008 NBA draft]] by the [[Phoenix Suns]], was traded to the [[New Orleans Hornets]] in 2012 and was traded to Portland in 2013. He played [[college basketball]] for the [[Stanford Cardinal men's basketball|Stanford Cardinal]] alongside his twin brother [[Brook Lopez]]. He played for nine NBA teams, including a three-year stint with the [[Chicago Bulls]] and two stints with the [[Milwaukee Bucks]].
